$$

Next, we group the $\sin^2 x$ and $\cos^2 x$ terms and simplify any matching factors.

$$
\begin{aligned}
& \sin^{2} x\cdot\left(-3\frac{\cos^{2} x}{\sin^{2} x}\right) \\ &\quad {}+\sin^{2} x\cdot\left(4\frac{1}{\sin x}\right) \\ &\quad {}-3\sin^{2} x \\ &= -3(\sin^{2} x+\cos^{2} x)+4\sin x
\end{aligned}
$$

Then, we use $\sin^2 x+\cos^2 x=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:

$$
\begin{aligned}
& -3(\sin^{2} x+\cos^{2} x)+4\sin x \\ &= 4 \sin x- 3
\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore, we conclude that

$$
\begin{aligned}
