$$
\begin{aligned}
& \cos^{2} x\cdot\left(4\frac{\sin^{2} x}{\cos^{2} x}\right) \\ &\quad {}+\cos^{2} x\cdot\left(-\frac{1}{\cos x}\right) \\ &\quad {}+4\cos^{2} x \\ &= 4(\cos^{2} x+\sin^{2} x)-\cos x
\end{aligned}
$$

Then, we use $\sin^2 x+\cos^2 x=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:

$$
\begin{aligned}
